  "circulationNotes": "The design prioritizes a clear, L-shaped peripheral circulation path around the central courtyard on the ground floor, enhancing natural light and ventilation. The dog-legged staircase serves as a prominent vertical connection, strategically placed to be easily accessible from both public and semi-private zones. Upstairs, the family lounge acts as a central hub, connecting all private bedrooms and the common bath.",
  "rationale": "This design for a 40x60 ft E-facing plot in Kochi, Kerala, explicitly addresses the brief by delivering a 3BHK, 2-story residence for a 5-member family. The 'courtyard_centered' planning type, strongly referencing traditional Kerala Nadumuttam architecture, is pivotal for climate-adaptive living. \n\n**Ground Floor (Level 0):** The Verandah and Formal Living are oriented East, welcoming morning sun and street connection. A central Foyer leads into the main living areas, which wrap around the 'Nadumuttam' (courtyard). This courtyard is vital for cross-ventilation and bringing in diffused light, reducing reliance on artificial cooling. The Dining and Kitchen are strategically placed on the North-East, adjacent to each other for functional efficiency. The Master Bedroom with its ensuite is tucked away on the quieter North-West side, offering privacy and natural coolness, aligning with aging-in-place principles. A common bathroom serves guests and the utility area. \n\n**First Floor (Level 1):** The staircase leads directly into a spacious Family Lounge, which overlooks the courtyard below, maintaining visual connectivity and vertical ventilation. Two additional bedrooms (Bedroom 2 & 3) are located on this floor, sharing a common bathroom, ensuring the 3-bedroom, 3-bathroom requirement (2+ specified minimum) is met. A balcony extends from the family lounge to the East, providing an outdoor breakout space. \n\n**Climate Adaptability & Style:** The courtyard, verandahs, and strategic window placements directly address Kochi's warm, humid climate. The overall L-shaped massing around the courtyard optimizes daylight and natural breeze. The chosen Kerala Traditional style is evident in the planning concept, promoting sustainable and culturally rich living. All mandatory space and room counts (3 bedrooms, 2 floors, 2+ bathrooms, 1 parking) have been strictly adhered to and integrated functionally within the site constraints.",
  "modeConsiderations": [
    {
      "mode": "climate_adaptive",
      "note": "The central Nadumuttam (courtyard) creates a natural stack effect for ventilation, drawing in cooler air and expelling hot air. East-facing verandahs and main living areas maximize beneficial morning sun and prevailing breezes, while minimizing direct harsh afternoon sun. Strategic shading and window placement further enhance thermal comfort and reduce energy consumption."
    }
  ],
